{"chunk_id": "0928624984b0", "text": "This section captures the explosive aftermath of the dice-game humiliation. Dussasana mocks the Pandavas openly in the Kuru court, provoking Bhima\u2019s fury. Bound by dharma and unable to act immediately, Bhima responds with terrible vows: he swears to tear open Dussasana\u2019s chest and drink his blood, and to destroy those who support the Kauravas. Duryodhana further insults him by mockingly imitating Bhima\u2019s gait, deepening the outrage. As the Pandavas depart, each brother declares a solemn oath of vengeance\u2014Bhima against Duryodhana and Dussasana, Arjuna against Karna, Sahadeva against Sakuni, and Nakula against the Kauravas who insulted Draupadi. These vows foreshadow the future war and define the personal targets that will shape the great battles of the Mahabharata.\nInsulted in the Kaurava court, the Pandavas swear deadly vows against their enemies before departing, while Yudhishthira formally bids farewell.\nThemes: vows of vengeance, honor and insult, brotherly resolve, foreshadowing war", "vector": [-0.015929073095321655, -0.013879327103495598, -0.0076430076733231544, 0.0010449686087667942, -0.017215188592672348, 0.023016102612018585, -0.025159629061818123, -0.01284105610102415, -0.01103245746344328, -0.03003614954650402, 0.016665909439325333, 0.005539673380553722, 0.02710219845175743, 0.0017516621155664325, 0.004384179133921862, 0.0050238873809576035, 0.04372791573405266, 0.002624143846333027, 0.04897955432534218, -0.020269712433218956, -0.003982268273830414, -0.004685612395405769, -0.0014560900162905455, 0.035662904381752014, -0.0255749374628067, 0.028401710093021393, 0.018461111932992935, -0.022386442869901657, 0.0012358763488009572, 0.002103334292769432, -0.003888488980010152, -0.006865979637950659, 0.006172683089971542, -0.002416489878669381, -0.03834230825304985, 0.007515735924243927, -0.017871642485260963, -0.024744320660829544, 0.02075200527906418, 0.0052851298823952675, 0.0007761906017549336, -0.01